      "headline": "Pinning Numbers on Foggy Fortunes",
      "keyInsight": "Pundits love words like 'distinct possibility' or 'looming crisis.' These phrases sound profound, but they are hollow masks. If an event happens, the pundit claims they foresaw it.\n\nIf it fails, they insist they only called it possible. To find truth, we must force slippery words into hard numbers.\n\nOnce you pin a forecast to an exact probability and date, excuses evaporate. Tracking real accuracy exposes a shocking reality: fame and certainty rarely equal foresight.\n\nRigorous scorekeeping strips away clever rhetoric and shows what brains actually know.",
