      "chapterOrder": 2,
      "title": "The Dart-Throwing Chimp Baseline",
      "prompt": "Tetlock found that human domain experts often perform roughly on par with a dart-throwing chimpanzee when predicting long-range scenarios. Identify a forecast or life assessment you made that failed noticeably. What baseline probability or random benchmark would you have been up against if you hadn't over-complicated the analysis?",
      "placeholder": "Describe a failed prediction and what a simple baseline distribution would have looked like instead..."
